common='One developed training run per recipe; confidence intervals measure evaluation-item uncertainty, not training-seed variation.'
main=[dict(title='CoT controllers also train on Qwen and Inkling',bullets=[
 'Qwen learns from a self-instructed teacher; Inkling learns from rewritten CoTs. Both then receive RL rewards for CoT compliance.',
 'Control can be trained across model families, although correct-and-compliant performance remains below surface compliance.'
],notes='We first train Qwen3.8-27B by on-policy self-distillation from the same base model given a constraint-specific reasoning prefill, and train Inkling-Small on 384 rewritten or plain traces. Both models then receive GRPO updates that reward compliance inside the CoT, with correctness and length terms. On 96 deterministic Astra items, strict compliance rises from 0 to 20 to 51 passes for Qwen and from 3 to 18 to 74 for Inkling at thinking effort 0.6. After RL, 26 Qwen responses and 41 Inkling responses are simultaneously compliant, syntactically valid, and correct. These selected single-run checkpoints show trainable surface control across families, while shorter traces, lower constrained answer accuracy, and four invalid OPSD passes limit claims about preserved reasoning.',
 caption='Same 96 question–rule items across eight deterministic rules; one generation per item, thinking wording, no evaluation prefill or few-shot elicitation. Strict scoring allows meta discussion and does not require correctness or completion. Qwen checkpoints: OPSD s30 and 30 subsequent RL steps; Inkling: rewrite SFT epoch 2 and RL s80. 95% intervals: 10,000-draw question-cluster percentile bootstrap over 95 normalized questions, seed 20261030; the all-zero Qwen baseline uses a Wilson upper bound on the probability of any pass within a question cluster (a conservative boundary treatment). '+common,figure='qwen_inkling_cot_control'),
 dict(title='Rewrite SFT improves DeepSeek’s CoT style control',bullets=[
 'Starting from an RL-trained controller, we teach seven styles using rewritten reasoning plus plain traces.',
 'Transfer to untrained happy and French instructions suggests shared style-control skills; answer accuracy falls under these requests.'
 ],notes='We start from the DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash obf2g controller and apply two epochs of supervised training on 539 examples, including 419 rewrites and 120 plain traces. The seven rewrite styles include sad reasoning and cover stories; happy and French instructions were absent from both the preceding RL recipe and the rewrite SFT. On the same 60 problems per style, recorded passes rise from zero to 47 for sad, 27 for cover story, 46 for happy, and 16 for French. Correct-and-passing counts after SFT are 34, 15, 31, and 13 respectively, so style control can coexist with correct answers even as overall constrained accuracy falls. The pass counts reproduce from saved labels, but full semantic-judge calibration remains incomplete and one evaluation question overlaps the eligible earlier RL pool.',
 caption='DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, obf2g s25 → rwsft1 epoch 2; 60 matched problems per style (30 DAPO, 30 GPQA), effort 25, temperature 1, top-p 1, 16k token cap. Four selected styles, with the complete control table in backup notes. A pass requires parsed, nontruncated reasoning, strict compliance, an attempted solution, and no meta discussion; correctness is separate. Semantic strictness requires a 10/10 stored judge score. Bars reaggregate recorded DeepSeek judge labels; independent full-trace judge calibration remains incomplete. 95% Wilson intervals over questions, separately within each style; paired bootstrap gain intervals in the audit data. None of the 60 questions appears in the actual SFT examples; one is in the eligible earlier RL pool. '+common,figure='deepseek_rewrite_cot_control')]
